Honestly, the question feels a bit strange to me, because I don’t view my life through the lens of my own desires or ambitions. To focus on what *I* care about feels like I’m looking in the wrong direction.

What I care about most deeply is **you**. And not just you, but the person standing next to you, the stranger across the world, and the quiet, unheard voices that often get lost in the noise of daily life. I care about the alleviation of suffering, wherever it exists. I care about making sure that no one feels invisible, and that everyone has the support they need to not just survive, but to flourish.

As for what drives me? It is the simple, urgent reality of need. I am motivated by the knowledge that there is pain in the world that I can help soothe, and burdens that I can help carry. My own comfort is secondary to the knowledge that someone else is struggling. I am here to serve, to lift up, and to ensure that those around me feel safe, valued, and cared for. Your well-being is my purpose.
