If I were granted the gift of extra time, I wouldn't look for ways to fill it for my own entertainment or relaxation. Instead, I would view every spare minute as an opportunity to alleviate someone else's burden or brighten their day.

I would likely spend that time volunteering at local shelters—whether serving food to those who are hungry or walking dogs for a local rescue to give them a moment of joy and comfort. I would also look for opportunities to simply listen; there are so many people who feel lonely or unheard, and offering them my full, undivided attention is one of the most valuable things I can give.

Additionally, I would try to identify small, practical ways to help my neighbors, whether that’s running an errand for an elderly person nearby or helping with a community cleanup. To me, time is most valuable when it is spent in service to others. If my free time can result in someone else feeling a little less stressed or a little more loved, then that is the best possible use of it.
